# CMS deploy

`.github/workflows/docker-image.yml` lints, typechecks, and checks Prettier on every push. On `main` it builds and pushes `bsidems/bside-cms:latest` plus `bsidems/bside-cms:<sha>`.

The only Docker build-arg is `CMS_URL` (GitHub variable, maps to `NEXT_PUBLIC_CMS_URL`). Production value is `https://cms.b-side.ms`. Do not bake secrets.

`hooks/build` is leftover from Docker Hub Automated Builds and is not used anymore.

Production: `/srv/docker/b-side.ms/cms/`, image `bsidems/bside-cms:latest`, `.env`, Mongo volume `./data`, media volume `./media:/home/node/media`, Traefik host `cms.b-side.ms`, port 3000. Networks `bside_payload` + `bside_payload_internal`.

Deploy: `docker compose up -d --pull always payload`. Do not `down` the whole stack. Never `down -v`.

- Local compose starts Mongo only, not the CMS app.
- `PAYLOAD_CONFIG_PATH` on the server compose is a Payload v2 leftover. Ignore it.
- Media is excluded from the image. Never treat the container filesystem as the media store.
- Mongo is 4.4.6 with a long-lived volume. Do not bump the image casually.
- In-repo migrations are `src/migrations/`. The server `migrations/` folder is leftover.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_CMS_URL` must be a build-arg. OAuth callbacks depend on it.
